MODI is an OpenAI powered chatbot built into my personal portfolio. It allows users to ask questions about my engineering projects, experience, and background in a conversational format.

So the UI is built using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. When a user sends a message, the frontend sends a POST request to a Flask backend ran by Render. 

The backend receives the message, sends it to the OpenAI API along with portfolio-specific context, and returns the generated response to the frontend.

The general architecture is:

The OpenAI API key is stored in .env file which is included in the .gitignore so the .env file is never exposed. 

The chatbot also includes suggested question buttons to help visitors explore the portfolio.

I used these tools:
- HTML
- CSS
- JavaScript
- Python
- Flask
- OpenAI API
- Render
- GitHub Pages
- Git / GitHub
- Claude Sonnet 5 VS Code extension


To run this locally open repo and terminal:
-------------------------
cd backend #Goes into the backend folder

#Creates a virtual Python environment named "venv"
python3 -m venv venv      

source venv/bin/activate # Activate the virtual environment

#Installs all Python packages required by the backend stated in the requirements.txt
pip install -r requirements.txt 

python3 app.py #Start the Flask backend locally
-------------------------


After starting, the backend runs at http://127.0.0.1:5000
The chatbot sends POST requests to http://127.0.0.1:5000/chat

I used ChatGPT 5.6 Sol to help me understand frontend and backend setup.